.TH MAPS-NDJSON-VIEWER 1 "9 September 2026" "maps-apps 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
maps-ndjson-viewer \- query decoded MAPS NDJSON message logs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B maps-ndjson-viewer
.I file-or-directory
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B maps-ndjson-viewer
loads MAPS message-log NDJSON through embedded DuckDB, decodes Base64 opaqueData,
and exposes decoded JSON for SQL analysis. Directories are searched recursively.
.PP
The relations maps_log and mavlink_log are available to queries. No external database
server or DuckDB installation is required.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --topics
List topics and record counts.
.TP
.BI --sql " query"
Execute DuckDB SQL against maps_log or mavlink_log.
.TP
.BI --database " file"
Persist the imported records in a DuckDB database file.
.TP
.BI --format " table|ndjson|csv"
Select the result format.
.TP
.BI --output " file"
Write results to a file. A .csv suffix selects CSV; other suffixes select NDJSON unless
--format is specified.
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
.TP
.B .topics
List all topics.
.TP
.B .mavlink-topics
List MAVLink topics.
.TP
.B .schema
Describe maps_log.
.TP
.B .quit
Exit the interactive shell.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/maps/apps/ndjson_viewer.jar
Executable JAR installed by the maps-apps Debian package.
.SH AUTHOR
MapsMessaging B.V.
